# 2️⃣ VECTORS

A vector is simply an ordered collection of numbers.

Example:

```text
x = [10, 20, 30]
```

We can represent it vertically:

$$
x=
\begin{bmatrix}
10\\
20\\
30
\end{bmatrix}
$$

This vector has:

```text
3 elements
```

Therefore its shape is:

$$
(3,)
$$

in NumPy's 1-D representation.

---

# 🧠 Real-world example

Suppose one student has:

```text
Age = 21
Study Hours = 5
Attendance = 90
```

Represent the student as:

$$
x =
\begin{bmatrix}
21\\
5\\
90
\end{bmatrix}
$$

That's a **feature vector**.

Machine learning models work heavily with feature vectors.

---

