# 4️⃣ MATRIX

A matrix is a rectangular arrangement of numbers.

Example:

$$
X=
\begin{bmatrix}
21 & 5 & 90\\
22 & 6 & 85\\
20 & 4 & 95
\end{bmatrix}
$$

We have:

```text
3 rows
3 columns
```

Therefore:

$$
Shape=(3,3)
$$

---

# 🧠 ML interpretation

Rows usually represent:

```text
observations / samples
```

Columns usually represent:

```text
features
```

So:

```text
X =

       Age  Study  Attendance
        ↓     ↓       ↓
       ┌────────────────────┐
Student│ 21    5      90    │
       │ 22    6      85    │
       │ 20    4      95    │
       └────────────────────┘
```

This is exactly how many ML datasets are represented.

