# 1️⃣1️⃣ `*` VS `@` ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

This is a very common Python/NumPy mistake.

### Element-wise multiplication

```python
A * B
```

means:

```text
element × corresponding element
```

Example:

```text
[1 2]
[3 4]

*

[5 6]
[7 8]
```

gives:

```text
[5  12]
[21 32]
```

---

### Matrix multiplication

```python
A @ B
```

performs mathematical matrix multiplication.

This distinction is **very important in ML code**.

