# 1️⃣6️⃣ LINEAR TRANSFORMATION

A matrix can transform vectors.

Suppose:

$$
x=
\begin{bmatrix}
1\\
2
\end{bmatrix}
$$

and:

$$
A=
\begin{bmatrix}
2&0\\
0&2
\end{bmatrix}
$$

Then:

$$
Ax=
\begin{bmatrix}
2\\
4
\end{bmatrix}
$$

The vector has effectively been scaled by 2.

```text
Before:

   ↗
  /
 /

After:

      ↗
     /
    /
```

Matrices can perform transformations such as:

* scaling
* rotation
* reflection
* projection

This becomes important later in:

* PCA
* computer vision
* neural networks
* embeddings
* dimensionality reduction

