# 1️⃣7️⃣ THE BIG ML CONNECTION 🔥🔥🔥

Now let's connect everything.

Suppose we have:

```text
1000 customers
5 features each
```

Our feature matrix:

$$
X=(1000\times5)
$$

Our model weights:

$$
W=(5\times1)
$$

Then:

$$
XW
$$

has shape:

$$
(1000\times1)
$$

Meaning:

```text
1000 customers
      ↓
Matrix multiplication
      ↓
1000 predictions
```

This is the power of linear algebra.

Instead of:

```python
for customer in customers:
    calculate_prediction()
```

we can perform a vectorized operation:

```python
predictions = X @ W
```

This is:

> **Vectorization**

And you already encountered vectorization during Day 2.

Now you can see **why it matters**.

