# 2️⃣1️⃣ COMMON MISTAKES 🚨

### Mistake 1

Using:

```python
A * B
```

when you actually need:

```python
A @ B
```

---

### Mistake 2

Ignoring shape.

Always check:

```python
print(X.shape)
print(W.shape)
```

---

### Mistake 3

Thinking:

```text
(3,4) @ (3,2)
```

works.

It doesn't.

Remember:

> **Inner dimensions must match.**

---

### Mistake 4

Confusing vector shape:

```text
(3,)
```

with:

```text
(3,1)
```

They are not identical objects in NumPy.

```python
x = np.array([1, 2, 3])

print(x.shape)
```

gives:

```text
(3,)
```

while:

```python
x = np.array([
    [1],
    [2],
    [3]
])

print(x.shape)
```

gives:

```text
(3,1)
```

This distinction becomes important in ML code.

