# 2️⃣2️⃣ 🎯 INTERVIEW QUESTIONS

### Q1. What is a vector?

> A vector is an ordered collection of numerical values that can represent quantities or features. In ML, a feature vector can represent one data sample.

---

### Q2. What is a matrix?

> A matrix is a rectangular arrangement of numbers organized into rows and columns. In ML, a matrix commonly represents a dataset where rows are samples and columns are features.

---

### Q3. Difference between dot product and matrix multiplication?

> A dot product combines corresponding elements of two compatible vectors and sums the products. Matrix multiplication generalizes this operation to matrices, where each output element is obtained from a row-column dot product.

---

### Q4. What is the difference between `*` and `@` in NumPy?

```text
* → element-wise multiplication
@ → matrix multiplication
```

---

### Q5. Why is linear algebra important in ML?

> ML models represent data, parameters, transformations, and predictions using vectors and matrices. Matrix operations allow models to process large numbers of features and samples efficiently through vectorized computation.

